/* 12MF - scoped operator correction; prior sources remain intact. */
var CF_SOURCE_12MF={"build":"12MF","date":"2026-10-22","title":"C-4100 / C-4200 - operator remote-capacity and controlled-shutdown correction","sourceClass":"OPERATOR_PROVIDED_CONTROL_BEHAVIOR","sourceFile":"Operator correction in conversation, 22 October 2026","ownerKeys":["c4100","c4200"],"equipmentIds":["C-4100","C-4200"],"notebookKey":"inlet_capacity_control_12mf","operatorStatement":"in the control screens remote capacity on inlet compressors when using + or - its up and down by 5% like 75 80 85, 80% is a normal when dropping it flow will be reduced and adding flow will increase both are slightly like maybe 1-3 mmscfd when unit gets shut down the capacity goes to 50% a controlled shut down the capacity starts at 80% after all load steps are taken out you drop capacity by 5 % until 50% is reached and then hit shut down","scope":"Inlet compressors only. Operator-provided simulator behavior, not independently verified PLC logic, OEM performance, or an approved field procedure. Residue and other compressor controls are unchanged.","newEntries":[{"id":"capacity_steps","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"text":"Remote Capacity + / - commands use a 5-percentage-point grid: 75%, 80%, 85%. 80% is the normal operating reference, not a permanently enforced live value."},{"id":"capacity_flow","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"text":"Lowering Remote Capacity reduces flow; raising it increases flow slightly. The operator estimates about 1-3 MMSCFD per 5-point change during normal loaded operation. This is approximate operating experience, not a guaranteed flow increment or a new limit."},{"id":"stop_reset","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"text":"When either inlet compressor shuts down, its Remote Capacity returns to 50%. Protective trips, ESD, blowdown-stop and maintenance stops remain immediate; they do not wait for a controlled unloading sequence."},{"id":"controlled_stop","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"text":"Operator-described controlled shutdown from normal 80%: remove all load steps first, then reduce Remote Capacity manually 80 -> 75 -> 70 -> 65 -> 60 -> 55 -> 50%, and only then press SHUTDOWN. Reaching Step 0 / 50% does not stop the driver automatically."},{"id":"simulation_qualification","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"authority":"SIMULATOR_IMPLEMENTATION_ASSUMPTION","text":"Simulator calibration: loaded inlet capacity trims by a nominal 2 MMSCFD per 5 percentage points (0.4 MMSCFD per point), within the operator estimate. Actual meter response remains subject to feed, recycle, pressure and downstream constraints and existing process lags. The retained Step-0 unloading ramp from 80% to zero modeled displacement at 50% is separate from the small loaded trim; the 1-3 estimate is not imposed on that whole unloading ramp. Existing load-step tables and residue equations are retained."},{"id":"shutdown_guard","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"authority":"SIMULATOR_TRAINING_GUARD","text":"In the simulator, normal SHUTDOWN requires Step 0 and Remote Capacity 50%; attempting it earlier displays the remaining preparation instead of automatically changing controls. Selecting 50% with load steps still applied asks for Step 0 first. These are training guards, not a newly verified field interlock. Existing START at Step 0 / 50% and its 80% load-step permissive are retained."},{"id":"legacy_seed","tags":["C-4100","C-4200"],"authority":"SIMULATOR_CALIBRATION_CHANGE","text":"The fresh-start inlet Remote Capacity is now 80%, replacing the former model-derived 78.005% seed. The historical 205.37 / 196.01 MMSCFD meter observation remains retained, not a forced steady-state target. At the unchanged Step-3 table, both inlet machines at 80% have 220 MMSCFD combined gross configured capacity before process constraints. Saved/history records are not rewritten; an off-grid restored command goes to the next 5-point grid value in the requested direction on its next click."}],"pending":["Exact measured per-unit capacity/flow response curve and field response time are not established by this approximate observation. No additional upload is required to apply this simulator correction."],"unchanged":["equipment identities","individual serial/NB ownership","geometry and piping","existing alarm/trip thresholds","residue compressor controls and equations","browser storage keys and history schemas","15 data scripts"]};
