var CF_SOURCE_12MQ={"build":"12MQ","baseline":"12MP","date":"2026-10-23","id":"frick_internal_training_12mq","title":"Equipment Internal Training - Frick propane module and detail review","notebookKey":"compressor_internals_training_12mo","sourceClass":"RETAINED_PLANT_RECORDS_WITH_SEPARATE_OEM_FAMILY_TRAINING_RESEARCH","sourceStorageMode":"learn-only","sourceMediaRetained":false,"ownerKeys":["c4100","c6100","c5700","c1141"],"equipmentIds":["C-4100","C-6100","C-5700","C-1141"],"intake":{"filename":"p_47_Frick-RWF-II-177-Compressor-Parts(3).pdf","sha256":"190ffc1632b00452d1a6594cd3cf8179a586f978346a939d9aa92a12fecd37e2","bytes":4735040,"pages":80,"decision":"EXACT_FILE_DUPLICATE_REUSE_CF_SOURCE_12KU","existingOwner":"CF_SOURCE_12KU","existingManualKey":"frick_rwfii_manual","visuallyReviewedPages":[2,4,6,7,18,22,23,24,26,46,47,57,58,59,60,66,69,70],"newManualFacts":0},"model":{"id":"refrigeration","kind":"screw","title":"Refrigeration","tag":"C-1141","owner":"c1141","family":"Frick RWF-546E / SGC 2824","throws":0,"stages":1,"cylinderKeys":[],"cylinderLabels":["Screw compression core","Separator and coalescers","Oil circulation","Hydraulic controls","Motor and coupling"],"stageMap":[1,1,1,1,1],"flowSummary":"Propane vapor -> suction check/strainer -> helical working pockets + injected oil -> discharge mixture -> PW-1101 bulk separation and coalescers -> propane discharge. Separate dry economizer vapor enters SV-1. Oil is recovered, cooled, filtered and returned.","sourceRefs":["CF_SOURCE_12LG","CF_SOURCE_12KP","CF_SOURCE_12LM","CF_SOURCE_12KU"],"qualification":"One representative, not a sister-unit serial copy. Plant package and element evidence are retained separately. Internal profile, routing geometry and slow-motion cycle are teaching approximations. No calibrated propane thermodynamic or oil-flow calculation."},"newEntries":[{"id":"mq_frick_scope","title":"One source-linked Frick refrigeration trainer","tags":["C-1141"],"text":"The representative is the existing C-1141 RWF-546E package and its retained SGC2824 element evidence, not a new RWF177 package inferred from the filename. Exact-owner identifiers and specifications are read from the current primary dossier. Package, element, driver and separator evidence remain separate."},{"id":"mq_rotors","title":"Rotating helical assembly","tags":["C-1141"],"text":"Official Frick 070.650-IOM (2022-02) describes a four-lobed male rotor connected to the driver and six-lobed female rotor driven on an oil film. The teaching pair rotates oppositely at the corresponding 4:6 lobe ratio. The constructed profile is illustrative, not a conjugate manufacturing profile, clearance measurement, or serial-specific internal drawing. Radial bearings, thrust-bearing groups, shaft seal and balance-piston roles have separate selectable groups.","researchId":"frick-rotors"},{"id":"mq_gas_oil","title":"Propane and oil remain different circuits","tags":["C-1141"],"text":"Use the current M2221B/C package owners for suction, dry economizer vapor, discharge mixture, horizontal PW-1101 separator, coalescing groups, duty/standby oil filters, cooler, pump and hydraulic connections. Colored moving markers illustrate direction, not mass flow. No liquid propane is shown as the normal main-suction feed; optional catalog liquid-injection ports remain capped reference provisions. No invented drain destination is joined to the gas or oil loop."},{"id":"mq_slide","title":"Capacity slide and volume-ratio slide stop are distinct","tags":["C-1141"],"text":"The independent teaching position controls move the capacity slide and separate slide stop. Opening the unloading passage returns gas toward suction before compression. The volume-ratio demonstration changes the conceptual discharge opening. Position and Vi displays are not plant commands, live readings, setpoints, calibration or a pressure-ratio prediction. Rewind reviews time rather than authorizing reverse shaft operation.","researchId":"frick-capacity"},{"id":"mq_parts","title":"Parts worksheet and manual reuse","tags":["C-1141"],"text":"The new PDF is byte-identical to the retained CF_SOURCE_12KU parts list. Existing catalog identifiers, variants and qualifications are reused by source link. Training manufacturerPartNumber, installedRating and evidence remain unassigned until exact installed evidence is reviewed. Figure 23 is filed as a generic catalog P&ID with an internal document/figure locator, not an invented issued drawing number."},{"id":"mq_recip_review","title":"Reciprocating trainer detail review","tags":["C-4100","C-6100","C-5700"],"text":"Added cutaway filter-core illustration, strainer basket, oil-line clamps and a transparent chain-drive guard to the existing teaching circuits. These are explanatory details, not new installed components, measured tubing schedules or ordering parts. Existing piston, crosshead, rod, valve, pressure-cycle and separate oil-circuit identifiers remain intact."},{"id":"mq_performance","title":"Rendering and picking work reduction","text":"The trainer reuses unchanged canvas dimensions, caches path distances, uses coarse-to-fine picking bounds, and selects reduced surface tessellation only for distant unselected circular primitives in the software renderer. All component identities and full-resolution geometry remain available when selected or close. Full plant speed is not certified by these local changes."},{"id":"mq_future","title":"Future equipment modules","text":"HMO heater and regeneration heater are visible future choices along with NGL pumps, expander and regeneration compressor. No internal heater animation, burner sequence or unverified combustion logic is presented as implemented."}],"research":[{"id":"frick-rotors","title":"Frick SGC rotor construction","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/General-Information/Construction-Details/Rotors","scope":"OEM family description: four male lobes and six female lobes; exact proprietary profile is not supplied.","accessed":"2026-10-23"},{"id":"frick-capacity","title":"Frick stepless capacity control","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/General-Information/Construction-Details/Stepless-capacity-control","scope":"Axial slide valve and suction recirculation before compression. A displayed position is not a calibrated installed flow percentage.","accessed":"2026-10-23"},{"id":"frick-vi","title":"Frick Volumizer volume-ratio control","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/General-Information/Construction-Details/Volumizer-variable-volume-ratio-control","scope":"Separate hydraulically moved slide stop; internal volume ratio is not the measured discharge/suction pressure ratio.","accessed":"2026-10-23"},{"id":"frick-oil","title":"Frick compressor lubrication system","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/General-Information/Description/Compressor-Lubrication-System","scope":"Oil functions for SGC; SGX-only squeeze-film options are not assigned to SGC2824.","accessed":"2026-10-23"},{"id":"frick-bearings","title":"Frick SGC bearings","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/General-Information/Construction-Details/Bearings","scope":"Radial roller and axial angular-contact bearing roles; quantities and clearances require installed drawings.","accessed":"2026-10-23"},{"id":"frick-hydraulic","title":"Frick hydraulic system","url":"https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/industrialrefrigeration/r/FRICK/en-US/SGC/SGX-Rotary-Screw-Compressor-IOM-MK2/2022-02/2022-02/Installation/Compressor-Hydraulic-System","scope":"Generic hydraulic principle, distinct from installed control commands and tuning.","accessed":"2026-10-23"}],"policy":["Use existing C-1141 records and source references; do not copy individual serial, order or National Board numbers to sister machines.","The 2013 parts list excludes special options, modifications and conversions. Catalog descriptions and candidates are not an installed bill of materials or service authorization.","No change to plant process equations, alarms, run states, valve states, password protection or existing storage schemas.","Internal geometry is a source-aware teaching abstraction. Exact rotor profiles, bearing stack, clearances, nozzle offsets, flow splits and packing/shaft seal parts require serial-specific evidence.","Existing owner-qualified cooled-oil PSV-1391 route remains separate from gas relief and does not discharge to flare. No relief setting is assigned by the trainer.","A demand oil pump animation is an explicit teaching selection, not proof that the pump runs continuously with the compressor.","Do not add SGC355-only SB-2 plumbing or SGX squeeze-film hardware to the SGC2824 illustration.","Rewind, pause, slide and Vi demonstrations affect only the private trainer clock. Future heater modules are disabled and no burner logic is implemented."],"pending":["Serial-specific SGC2824 rotor profile and bearing/seal assembly drawings, parts revisions and exact installed ratings.","Installed tubing sizes, hydraulic configuration and lube-flow distribution where not established by retained source-owned M2221B/C records.","Native WebGL/full-plant performance, rendered picking and end-to-end deployment remain separately testable; local fixtures do not certify them."],"drawings":[{"number":"FRICK-070.610-SPL-201307-FIG23","title":"Frick RWF II Figure 23 - typical piping and instrumentation","revision":"JUL 2013 catalog edition","pages":[58,59,60],"sourceFile":"p_47_Frick-RWF-II-177-Compressor-Parts(3).pdf","sha256":"190ffc1632b00452d1a6594cd3cf8179a586f978346a939d9aa92a12fecd37e2","referenceKey":"frick_rwfii_fig23_12mq","sourceClass":"GENERIC_VENDOR_REFERENCE_NOT_AS_BUILT","scope":"Internal catalog locator only; not an issued plant/vendor drawing number. Source engineering facts are retained once in CF_SOURCE_12KU. Typical options are not installed configurations.","existingManualKey":"frick_rwfii_manual","sourceStorageMode":"learn-only","sourceRetained":false}]};
